outlook.narrative:
Demand will keep rising as the population ages. Eurostat projections in the OECD profile put the share of people aged 65 and over at 28 percent by 2050, and 49 percent of those over 65 already lived with multiple chronic conditions in 2022.{{1}}

Money is the main constraint. The 2026 stabilization law, in force since 30 July 2026, limits spending growth across the health system, raises co-payments by 50 percent and answers a needed saving of almost €19 billion (US$21.3 billion) for 2027.{{2}}{{3}} The estimators' panel expects the average additional contribution to hold at 2.9 percent in 2027, but the health minister said the strain on insurers persists and structural problems must still be solved.{{4}}

Structural reform continues. Adjustments to the hospital reform give the Länder more time and delay the full effect of fixed capacity payments until 2030.{{5}} A primary care system with first effects expected in 2028 is being drafted, and the electronic patient record, opened to all doctors nationwide in April 2025, is meant to connect care settings.{{6}}{{7}}
